\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pills Prescribed By Pharmacists Broaden Effort in Fight on Access\b0\par\par\uc2 By Pam Belluck \par \uc2 1,303 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 January 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 17\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Washington State's program is the first, but other states are expected to try allowing pharmacists to prescribe the pills to counter growing efforts to curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Pharmacists have begun prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, not simply dispensing the medication -- a development intended to broaden \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access by taking advantage of rules that give them prescribing ability in most states.\par \par \uc2 The new effort is small so far -- a pilot program in Washington State -- but the idea is expected to be tried in other states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal.\par \par \uc2 ''I think it is going to expand, and it is expanding,'' said Michael Hogue, chief executive of the \uc2 American Pharmacists Association\uc2 , a national professional organization, which is not involved in the new program and does not take a position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nearly 40 states now allow pharmacists to prescribe at least some medications and they are trained to do so, he said. He added that in his organization's view, it makes sense to have ''someone so accessible in a local community be able to provide safe access to therapies that might sometimes be difficult to get.''\par \par \uc2 Supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights consider pharmacist prescribing part of an effort to open as many avenues as possible at a time when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills are facing growing attacks from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents.\par \par \uc2 Pharmacists are regulated by states, so their ability to prescribe specific medications cannot be blocked by the federal government. But if the incoming Trump administration wanted to stop pharmacists from prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, it could try to reinstate Food and Drug Administration regulations that required that only doctors prescribe mifepristone, the first pill in the two-drug medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimen.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists said they opposed the prescribing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by pharmacists, calling the practice reckless and unsafe.\par \par \uc2 ''Pharmacists, who do not receive clinical training, should not be distributing these dangerous drugs,'' Dr. Ingrid Skop, vice president and director of medical affairs at the Charlotte Lozier Institute, an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organization, said in a statement. ''By pushing these medically unsupervised abortions, the F.D.A. and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates continue down the slippery slope of chipping away at medical standards for women seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .''\par \par \uc2 Pills are now the method used in nearly two-thirds of abortions in the United States, and many studies have shown that medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is safe and that serious complications are rare.\par \par \uc2 Rules governing medication prescribing by pharmacists vary by state. Some allow prescribing for only a specific class or classes of drugs. Some require doctors to sign off on each prescription. Washington State's is considered the most lenient, requiring only that doctors approve the overall prescribing protocol and training.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Hogue of the pharmacists' association said that during the coronavirus pandemic, when access to doctors for nonemergency care was often limited or delayed, patients became accustomed to pharmacists' writing prescriptions. In many states, he said, pharmacists can prescribe birth control and morning-after pills.\par \par \uc2 But a lawsuit intended to force the F.D.A. to sharply restrict mifepristone was recently revived after the Supreme Court turned away the case, saying the original plaintiffs lacked the standing to sue.\par \par \uc2 The Texas attorney general recently sued an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in New York for sending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to a patient in Texas. And \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters are concerned that a 151-year-old federal anti-vice law known as the Comstock Act could be invoked by the incoming Trump administration to try to prevent the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication.\par \par \uc2 ''Attacks on access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care have created an urgent medical, public health and human rights crisis,'' said Dr. Beth Rivin, who leads a Seattle-based global health nonprofit, Uplift International, and is the managing director of the new program, called the Pharmacist \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Project. ''Even in Washington State, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal, people still face barriers to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, especially people who are struggling to make ends meet, live in rural areas and don't have easy access to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.''\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the Pharmacist \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Project reported that in a pilot program conducted between Oct. 31 and Nov. 26, 10 pharmacists across Washington State had prescribed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to 43 patients.\par \par \uc2 The prescribing was done via telehealth screening, with patients completing forms asking about their pregnancy and medical history. Patients had to be Washington residents and could be up to 10 weeks pregnant. They paid $40, significantly less than many services. Prescriptions were transmitted to Honeybee Health, a California-based mail-order pharmacy that works with many telemedicine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, which shipped the pills to patients.\par \par \uc2 Don Downing, a co-director of the project and a professor emeritus of pharmacy at the \uc2 University of Washington\uc2 , said that in addition to providing a hotline for questions or concerns, pharmacists had contacted patients to see how they were doing, asking questions like: ''Have you had excessive bleeding or no bleeding? Do you have fever, pain, whatever?''\par \par \uc2 He said that during the follow-up, patients had asked typical questions, like whether they were experiencing appropriate levels of bleeding from passing the pregnancy tissue. ''We did not have any seriously negative outcomes at all, but we had a full network of other resources available in case that happened, so that we could take care of them,'' he said.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Rivin said the project intends for full-fledged pharmacist prescribing to start sometime this year and to eventually allow in-person prescribing in Washington pharmacies, meaning patients could go to a pharmacy and receive a prescription and pills in one visit.\par \par \uc2 That would work in tandem with a recent F.D.A. policy allowing pharmacies to become certified to dispense mifepristone, which falls under a special regulatory regimen that previously required that it be dispensed primarily by clinics or other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services. The second drug in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimen, misoprostol, is less restricted and has long been widely available.\par \par \uc2 Last year, \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  and CVS began dispensing mifepristone in some states, as did scores of smaller pharmacies in at least a dozen states.\par \par \uc2 Brian Noble, chief executive of the Family Policy Institute of Washington and an evangelical pastor, said he was not opposed to pharmacists' prescribing medications in general or counseling women who are deciding whether to continue a pregnancy. But, he said, ''I'm against anything that ends life,'' which he believes begins at conception.\par \par \uc2 ''I believe in the aborted babies' rights,'' Mr. Noble said, adding, ''I see that women have the great privilege to be entrusted to carry life in their bodies.''\par \par \uc2 Jessica Nouhavandi, a pharmacist and president of Honeybee Health, who is a co-director of the new project, said she had come up with the idea of pharmacists prescribing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills several years ago because ''we need more providers, and we need it to be more accessible and more inexpensive.''\par \par \uc2 Dr. Nouhavandi said the project's patient consultation form asked for slightly more information than \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services where doctors or nurse practitioners issue prescriptions. ''We went a little deeper about medical history,'' she said. ''We wanted our pharmacists to feel more comfortable.''\par \par \uc2 The protocol was filed with the state's Health Department and was approved by an obstetrician-gynecologist, Dr. Downing said. He said the pharmacists in the pilot project had day jobs working for various employers, including chain and community pharmacies, hospitals and insurance companies. They prescribed for the pilot in their spare time and did not want to be identified.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Downing, who has pioneered other prescribing programs that have spread nationally, said other states might need to make changes to their regulations or laws to allow pharmacists to prescribe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. Still, he said, ''if, in fact, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in a state, I don't think there are too many impossible barriers.''\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250108el180003g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
