\par\par \uc2 MAUREEN DOWD\par \uc2 Editorial Desk; SECTSR\par \b \uc2 JD Smirks His Way Into the Future\b0\par\par\uc2 By Maureen Dowd \par \uc2 1,003 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 When I've covered the campaigns of women on presidential tickets, the question invariably arises: ''Is she tough enough to be commander in chief?''\par \par \uc2 With the bubbly Geraldine Ferraro, a lot of voters had their doubts.\par \par \uc2 There was less worry with \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 . She was a gold-plated hawk who voted to let President \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2  invade Iraq and persuaded President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  to join in bombing Muammar el-Qaddafi's Libya.\par \par \uc2 It is not surprising, with cascading conflicts, that Republicans are leveling the toughness question at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . This week the Trump/Vance campaign released an ad called ''Weakness.'' (\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also ran an ad called ''Weakness'' against \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , a hawk.)\par \par \uc2 The ad's subtext is clearly gender, trying to exploit Kamala's problems winning over Black and white working-class men.\par \par \uc2 In a Times/Siena College poll last month, 55 percent of respondents said Trump was respected by foreign leaders while 47 percent said that of Harris.\par \par \uc2 The ad claims Harris is not tough enough to deal with China, Russia, Iran or \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . It features actors playing \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , \uc2 Hamas\uc2  fighters and a tea-sipping ayatollah watching videos of the candidate who wants to be the first woman president. It ends with four clips of Kamala dancing -- a lot better than Trump does -- and a clip of Trump walking on a tarmac with a military officer and a Secret Service agent. The tag line is: ''America doesn't need another TikTok performer. We need the strength that will protect us.''\par \par \uc2 Even though Trump lives in a miasma of self-pity and his businesses often ended up in bankruptcy, somehow his fans mistake his swagger and sneers for machismo. What a joke. Trump is the one who caves, a foreign policy weakling and stooge of Putin.\par \par \uc2 This weekend, he is martyr-milking the one moment where he did show courage, the assassination attempt in Butler, Pa., by returning to the crime scene and treating it as hallowed ground for his quasi-religious lion imagery. After vowing at the convention to never discuss the event again -- ''It's actually too painful to tell'' -- he wants to wallow in accolades from \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and JD Vance, and sell more of his $299 ''FIGHT FIGHT FIGHT'' high-tops depicting his bloody face and raised fist.\par \par \uc2 His new ad slams Harris for ''anti-Israel statements'' that \uc2 Hamas\uc2  will use as a green light ''to keep murdering Israelis.''\par \par \uc2 But Harris has said she would always stand up for Israel's right to defend itself and she praised Israel's killing of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  leader \uc2 Hassan Nasrallah\uc2 , saying he was ''a terrorist with American blood on his hands.''\par \par \uc2 She has, however, shown more sympathy for Palestinians than has Joe Biden. In a Trumpworld that thrives on mendacity, demonizing and dividing, sympathy is weakness.\par \par \uc2 Unless you need to fake it to improve your favorability numbers -- like Vance did in his debate against \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 David Axelrod had predicted it would be a match between a Labrador retriever and a coyote. But there were two Labs onstage.\par \par \uc2 Vance's performance was chilling. Once I thought Trump would be an aberration for Republicans. But on Tuesday night, I saw the future of the party and it was lies piled on lies, and darkness swallowing darkness.\par \par \uc2 Vance seemed like a replicant. There was no sign of the smarmy right-wing troll who said Harris ''can go to hell'' and told CNN's Dana Bash that he created stories about migrants eating cats and dogs to dramatize a narrative that helps the Republican ticket. (A racist narrative.)\par \par \uc2 His views against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are adamantine and, until recently, he was an I.V.F. opponent. He has a bizarre, degrading view of the role of women in American society.\par \par \uc2 But on Tuesday night, he put on a mask of likability and empathy. ''Christ have mercy, it is awful,'' Vance said, looking down and shaking his head, when Walz told of his teenage son witnessing a shooting.\par \par \uc2 The chameleon brought back the JD Vance who was the darling of Hollywood, when ''Hillbilly Elegy'' was made into a movie, before he ambitiously code-switched into a Trumper. His wife, Usha, a debate adviser, helped him craft a persona that made him more palatable to women.\par \par \uc2 He was wily and deceptive in how he talked about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , stressing that women needed ''options'' and sending his love to an old friend who he said had had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 One woman in the CNN focus group was impressed with his empathy and talk of options, saying she was surprised and encouraged that Vance sounded so ''progressive.''\par \par \uc2 But before the 40-year-old JD teamed up with the 78-year-old Donald, his \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  position was draconian. For women in the wrong states, the need to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a terrifying prospect that could lead to death, if you are denied the proper treatment. And treatment is harder to get because doctors fear going to jail.\par \par \uc2 It's remarkable, given Vance's compassionate tone in his book, and his plea that the people of Appalachia be understood rather than ridiculed, how easily he morphed into someone with no compassion, stereotyping migrants and women.\par \par \uc2 After nearly 90 minutes of being lulled by Vance's sham persona, Walz finally ripped his opponent's mask off when Vance refused to say Trump lost the last election.\par \par \uc2 ''Tim,'' Vance protested, ''I'm focused on the future.''\par \par \uc2 It was the truest thing Vance said in a night of lying about his own positions and mythical Trump achievements.\par \par \uc2 Vance was focused on the future -- his own.\par \par \uc2 The Times is committed to publishing a diversity of letters to the editor. We'd like to hear what you think about this or any of our articles. Here are some tips . And here's our email: letters@nytimes.com .\par \par \uc2 Follow the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  Opinion section on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  , \uc2 Instagram\uc2  , TikTok , WhatsApp , X and Threads .\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020241006eka60004k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
