\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Fact-Checking the Debate\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kate Zernike, Coral Davenport, Sheryl Gay Stolberg, Ana Swanson, Linda Qiu, Lisa Friedman, Edward Wong, Julian E. Barnes, Jeanna Smialek, Andrew Duehren and Dana Goldstein \par \uc2 3,209 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ''The statute you signed into law, it\par \par \uc2 says that a doctor who presides over\par \par \uc2 an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  where the baby survives\par \par \uc2 -- the doctor is under no obligation\par \par \uc2 to provide lifesaving care to a baby\par \par \uc2 who survives a botched late-term\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .''\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE OF OHIO\par \par \uc2 This is false.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vance is distorting Mr. Walz's repeal\par \par \uc2 of a so-called born alive law that had\par \par \uc2 been in effect in Minnesota since the\par \par \uc2 1970s. That law required doctors to report\par \par \uc2 when a ''live child'' was ''born as the\par \par \uc2 result of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,'' and to provide ''all\par \par \uc2 reasonable measures consistent with\par \par \uc2 good medical practice'' to care for that infant.\par \par \uc2 Doctors have argued to get rid of these\par \par \uc2 laws because there are already laws requiring\par \par \uc2 them to provide appropriate\par \par \uc2 medical care to any human. And the extremely\par \par \uc2 rare cases of infants who have\par \par \uc2 been ''born alive'' were infants who were\par \par \uc2 close to death. Doctors said the law took\par \par \uc2 decision-making away from families,\par \par \uc2 and forced them to do invasive procedures\par \par \uc2 at the end of infants' lives, taking\par \par \uc2 them away from their parents in their dying\par \par \uc2 moments.\par \par \uc2 In the five years that Mr. Walz has\par \par \uc2 been governor, there have been eight recorded\par \par \uc2 infants ''born alive'': Three were\par \par \uc2 classified as ''previable,'' meaning they\par \par \uc2 were unable to survive outside the uterus;\par \par \uc2 two had fetal anomalies and died\par \par \uc2 shortly after birth; and three were provided\par \par \uc2 ''comfort care as planned'' and died\par \par \uc2 shortly after birth. Comfort care is a kind\par \par \uc2 of hospice care, which suggests that\par \par \uc2 those infants were not expected to survive,\par \par \uc2 and that doctors did, in fact, provide\par \par \uc2 care they believed to be good medical\par \par \uc2 practice. KATE ZERNIKE\par \par \uc2 ''We are the cleanest economy in the entire world.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This is false.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vance used this version of a line that\par \par \uc2 is often repeated by former President\par \par \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  and other Republicans\par \par \uc2 when asked what they would do to address\par \par \uc2 climate change. In fact, 15 countries\par \par \uc2 have cleaner air than the United\par \par \uc2 States, and 25 countries have cleaner\par \par \uc2 water, according to the Environmental\par \par \uc2 Performance Index, a global tracker run\par \par \uc2 by \uc2 Yale University\uc2 . During the Trump administration,\par \par \uc2 the United States rolled\par \par \uc2 back or eliminated nearly 100 clean air,\par \par \uc2 water and climate rules.\par \par \uc2 CORAL DAVENPORT\par \par \uc2 ''Project 2025 is going to have aregistry of pregnancies.''\par \par \uc2 GOV. TIM WALZ OF MINNESOTA\par \par \uc2 This is false.\par \par \uc2 Project 2025, a blueprint for governing\par \par \uc2 drafted by the conservative Heritage\par \par \uc2 Foundation, does not specifically call for\par \par \uc2 a ''registry of pregnancies,'' but it does\par \par \uc2 call for existing federal agencies to collect\par \par \uc2 more accurate data about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has distanced itself\par \par \uc2 from Project 2025. Mr. Walz is referring\par \par \uc2 to the project's proposal for the federal\par \par \uc2 Department of Health and Human\par \par \uc2 Services to ''use every available tool, including\par \par \uc2 the cutting of funds,'' to collect\par \par \uc2 data from states about abortions performed\par \par \uc2 within their borders.\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and\par \par \uc2 Prevention has collected data about\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1969, four years before the\par \par \uc2 1973 Supreme Court decision in Roe v.\par \par \uc2 Wade made the procedure legal across\par \par \uc2 the nation. But data reporting is voluntary.\par \par \uc2 Project 2025 calls for the \uc2 C.D.C.\uc2  to\par \par \uc2 ''require monitoring and reporting for\par \par \uc2 complications due to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .''\par \par \uc2 SHERYL GAY STOLBERG\par \par \uc2 ''Those same experts for 40 years\par \par \uc2 said that if we shipped our\par \par \uc2 manufacturing base off to China,\par \par \uc2 we'd get cheaper goods. They lied\par \par \uc2 about that.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This is false.\par \par \uc2 Outsourcing manufacturing from the\par \par \uc2 United States to other countries had documented\par \par \uc2 negative effects, like reducing\par \par \uc2 U.S. manufacturing employment and\par \par \uc2 suppressing American wages, but one\par \par \uc2 thing it did do is drastically lower the cost\par \par \uc2 of goods. Offshoring manufacturing allowed\par \par \uc2 companies to pay lower wages\par \par \uc2 and therefore charge American consumers\par \par \uc2 far less for their products like\par \par \uc2 shoes, electronics, clothing and toys.\par \par \uc2 Economic studies have found that, in the\par \par \uc2 years following China's entry into the\par \par \uc2 World Trade Organization\uc2  in 2001, U.S.\par \par \uc2 prices fell substantially. ANA SWANSON\par \par \uc2 ''Look, Tim, first of all, it's really rich\par \par \uc2 for Democratic leaders to say that\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a unique threat to\par \par \uc2 democracy when he peacefully gave\par \par \uc2 over power on January the 20th as\par \par \uc2 we have done for 250 years in this\par \par \uc2 country.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This is misleading.\par \par \uc2 While Mr. Trump did indeed leave office\par \par \uc2 on Jan. 20, 2021, without any violence,\par \par \uc2 that of course followed Mr. Trump's supporters\par \par \uc2 storming the Capitol on Jan. 6.\par \par \uc2 And though Mr. Trump and his allies continue\par \par \uc2 to falsely claim that congressional\par \par \uc2 proceedings on Jan. 6 to certify Electoral\par \par \uc2 College results remained ''peaceful,'' the\par \par \uc2 riot resulted in injuries to about 150 federal\par \par \uc2 and local police officers, several\par \par \uc2 deaths and $1.5 million in damages to the\par \par \uc2 Capitol. And fear of additional violence\par \par \uc2 led President Biden's inauguration that\par \par \uc2 year to include a large presence of armed\par \par \uc2 forces, as 25,000 National Guard troops\par \par \uc2 joined thousands of police officers.\par \par \uc2 LINDA QIU\par \par \uc2 ''This idea that carbon emissions\par \par \uc2 drives all of climate change -- let's\par \par \uc2 just say that's true, just for the sake\par \par \uc2 of argument.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This is misleading.\par \par \uc2 As he took issue with Vice President Kamala\par \par \uc2 Harris's climate agenda, Mr. Vance\par \par \uc2 was implying that the notion that carbon\par \par \uc2 emissions were the main cause of climate\par \par \uc2 change was false. In fact, carbon\par \par \uc2 emissions are driving climate change.\par \par \uc2 That is an established scientific fact,\par \par \uc2 backed up by the world's top scientists in\par \par \uc2 multiple United Nations-led reports, as\par \par \uc2 well as an exhaustive scientific report\par \par \uc2 the Trump administration issued in 2017.\par \par \uc2 The finding: Humans are the dominant\par \par \uc2 cause of the global temperature rise that\par \par \uc2 has created the warmest period in the\par \par \uc2 history of civilization. LISA FRIEDMAN\par \par \uc2 ''All I said on this is I got there this\par \par \uc2 summer and misspoke on this. So I\par \par \uc2 will just -- that's what I've said. So I\par \par \uc2 was in Hong Kong and China,\par \par \uc2 during the democracy protests, went\par \par \uc2 in. And from that, I learned a lot of\par \par \uc2 what needed to be in governance.''\par \par \uc2 MR. WALZ\par \par \uc2 This is misleading.\par \par \uc2 The pro-democracy protests in Beijing\par \par \uc2 and other cities in Communist-ruled\par \par \uc2 China peaked in the spring of 1989 and\par \par \uc2 ended when the Chinese military attacked\par \par \uc2 protesters overnight from June 3\par \par \uc2 to June 4, killing hundreds or thousands\par \par \uc2 of civilians around Tiananmen Square in\par \par \uc2 Beijing alone.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walz had plans to go to China in\par \par \uc2 August 1989, according to newspaper articles\par \par \uc2 from Nebraska that year. He has\par \par \uc2 said he went to China through Hong\par \par \uc2 Kong, which was a British colony then\par \par \uc2 and where residents held rallies to support\par \par \uc2 the pro-democracy protesters in\par \par \uc2 China, even after the military crackdown.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walz would not have seen the large\par \par \uc2 protests in the People's Republic that\par \par \uc2 people commonly think of as the pro-democracy\par \par \uc2 protests in China of 1989. He\par \par \uc2 would have arrived after their tragic end.\par \par \uc2 EDWARD WONG\par \par \uc2 ''Iran, which launched this attack,\par \par \uc2 has received over $100 billion in\par \par \uc2 unfrozen assets thanks to the\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  administration.\par \par \uc2 What did they use that money for?\par \par \uc2 They used it to buy weapons that\par \par \uc2 they are now launching against our\par \par \uc2 allies and God forbid, potentially\par \par \uc2 launching against the United States\par \par \uc2 as well.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This is misleading.\par \par \uc2 Give Mr. Vance credit for making this accusation\par \par \uc2 more accurately than Donald\par \par \uc2 Trump. Mr. Trump usually accuses President\par \par \uc2 Biden of giving Iran $150 billion of\par \par \uc2 taxpayer money. Mr. Vance used a smaller\par \par \uc2 number and made clear the money\par \par \uc2 was Iranian assets that had been previously\par \par \uc2 frozen in overseas accounts.\par \par \uc2 Those accounts were frozen as part of\par \par \uc2 international sanctions on Iran's nuclear\par \par \uc2 program, and some -- around $55 billion\par \par \uc2 -- was unfrozen as part of the original\par \par \uc2 Iran nuclear deal negotiated by the\par \par \uc2 Obama administration that was eventually\par \par \uc2 canceled by Mr. Trump. Ms. Harris\par \par \uc2 was not part of the Obama administration\par \par \uc2 that made the original Iran deal. The\par \par \uc2 Biden administration did not revive the\par \par \uc2 deal, did not unfreeze other accounts and\par \par \uc2 did not lift sanctions on Iran.\par \par \uc2 JULIAN E. BARNES\par \par \uc2 ''\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hasn't paid anyfederal tax 10 to the last 15 years.''\par \par \uc2 MR. WALZ\par \par \uc2 This is exaggerated.\par \par \uc2 A 2020 New York Times investigation\par \par \uc2 found that former Mr. Trump paid just\par \par \uc2 $750 in federal income taxes in 2016 and\par \par \uc2 another $750 in 2017, and he paid no income\par \par \uc2 taxes at all in 10 of the 15 previous\par \par \uc2 years. Since then, however, Democrats\par \par \uc2 made public more of Mr. Trump's tax\par \par \uc2 records, which show that his tax bill has\par \par \uc2 increased. During the first three years of\par \par \uc2 his presidency, he paid $1.1 million in federal\par \par \uc2 income taxes. In 2020, he again paid\par \par \uc2 no federal income taxes. LINDA QIU\par \par \uc2 ''25 million illegal aliens competing\par \par \uc2 with Americans for scarce homes is\par \par \uc2 one of the most significant drivers of\par \par \uc2 home prices in the country.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This is exaggerated.\par \par \uc2 Economists and real estate experts say\par \par \uc2 that while migration, including illegal\par \par \uc2 immigration, has contributed to population\par \par \uc2 growth and thus demand for housing,\par \par \uc2 it is not a main driver behind the\par \par \uc2 country's housing affordability crisis.\par \par \uc2 A lack of supply is the primary culprit,\par \par \uc2 they said. Mr. Vance also overestimated\par \par \uc2 how many unauthorized migrants have\par \par \uc2 entered and settled in the country. While\par \par \uc2 border crossings topped 10 million under\par \par \uc2 the Biden-Harris administration, many\par \par \uc2 of those migrants were turned away at\par \par \uc2 the border and many crossings were\par \par \uc2 from ''repeat offenders.'' LINDA QIU\par \par \uc2 ''Right now in this country,\par \par \uc2 Margaret, we have 320,000\par \par \uc2 children that the Department of\par \par \uc2 Homeland Security has effectively\par \par \uc2 lost. Some of them have been sex\par \par \uc2 trafficked.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This is misleading.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vance is wildly distorting a number\par \par \uc2 from a recent inspector general report.\par \par \uc2 The report noted that Immigrations\par \par \uc2 and Customs Enforcement transferred\par \par \uc2 some 448,000 unaccompanied migrant\par \par \uc2 children into the custody of the Health\par \par \uc2 and Human Services Department from\par \par \uc2 the 2019 to 2023 fiscal years. It did not issue\par \par \uc2 ''notices to appear'' in immigration\par \par \uc2 court to some 291,000 children. And\par \par \uc2 about 32,000 unaccompanied migrant\par \par \uc2 children failed to appear for their immigration\par \par \uc2 hearings.\par \par \uc2 In other words, that figure includes\par \par \uc2 both some 32,000 children who did not\par \par \uc2 appear for court hearings and the nearly\par \par \uc2 300,000 others who were not required to.\par \par \uc2 These children were not ''lost,'' nor is\par \par \uc2 there any evidence that they were sex\par \par \uc2 trafficked. Moreover, about half of that\par \par \uc2 time -- the 2019 and 2020 fiscal years,\par \par \uc2 and part of the 2021 fiscal year -- occurred\par \par \uc2 under the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 LINDA QIU\par \par \uc2 ''What [Harris has] actually done\par \par \uc2 instead is drive the cost of food\par \par \uc2 higher by 25 percent, drive the cost\par \par \uc2 of housing higher by about 60\par \par \uc2 percent.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This is misleading.\par \par \uc2 Both food and gas prices are up sharply\par \par \uc2 in recent years, though the commonly\par \par \uc2 used S&P CoreLogic Case Shiller Home\par \par \uc2 Price index is up less than 60 percent --\par \par \uc2 about 38 percent since the Biden administration\par \par \uc2 took office. But neither of those\par \par \uc2 jumps is solely because of administration\par \par \uc2 policies. Food prices were affected\par \par \uc2 by factors including Russia's invasion of\par \par \uc2 Ukraine and one-off issues like egg\par \par \uc2 shortages thanks to avian flu, and the\par \par \uc2 rapid housing price increase started under\par \par \uc2 the Trump administration and came\par \par \uc2 amid a persistent shortage of housing\par \par \uc2 supply. JEANNA SMIALEK\par \par \uc2 ''I never supported a national ban. I\par \par \uc2 did when I was running for Senate\par \par \uc2 talk about a minimum national\par \par \uc2 standard.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This needs context.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vance supported a national ban on\par \par \uc2 abortions after 15 weeks during his 2022\par \par \uc2 campaign for the Senate, but said he\par \par \uc2 would allow for some exceptions. ''I think\par \par \uc2 it's totally reasonable to say you cannot\par \par \uc2 abort a baby, especially for elective reasons,\par \par \uc2 after 15 weeks of gestation,'' he said\par \par \uc2 during a debate that year. LINDA QIU\par \par \uc2 ''\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was the guy who\par \par \uc2 created the largest trade deficit in\par \par \uc2 American history with China.''\par \par \uc2 MR. WALZ\par \par \uc2 The U.S. trade deficit in goods and services\par \par \uc2 with China hit a record peak in 2018,\par \par \uc2 when Mr. Trump was in office, at $378 billion.\par \par \uc2 It then shrank for the next two years of\par \par \uc2 the Trump administration, before rising\par \par \uc2 again after Mr. Biden took office, largely\par \par \uc2 because of the aftershocks of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Its highest level under Mr. Biden\par \par \uc2 was $366 billion in 2022. Last year, the\par \par \uc2 trade deficit with China fell sharply to\par \par \uc2 $252 billion, the lowest level in more than\par \par \uc2 a decade. But these fluctuations in the\par \par \uc2 trade deficit were most likely because of\par \par \uc2 broader economic factors, not solely\par \par \uc2 Trump or Biden administration policies.\par \par \uc2 ANA SWANSON\par \par \uc2 ''If you look at what was so different\par \par \uc2 about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's tax cuts, even\par \par \uc2 from previous Republican tax cut\par \par \uc2 plans, is that a lot of those resources\par \par \uc2 went to giving more take-home pay\par \par \uc2 to middle-class and working-class\par \par \uc2 Americans.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This needs context.\par \par \uc2 The 2017 tax cut signed into law by Mr.\par \par \uc2 Trump did provide a tax cut to many middle-\par \par \uc2 class and working-class households.\par \par \uc2 But the benefits from the tax cut largely\par \par \uc2 flowed to upper-income Americans.\par \par \uc2 According to an analysis by the Tax\par \par \uc2 Policy Center, more than 65 percent of\par \par \uc2 the tax cut accrued to the top 20 percent\par \par \uc2 of households. The bottom quintile of\par \par \uc2 American households was estimated to\par \par \uc2 receive a boost of 0.4 percent in after-tax\par \par \uc2 income because of the cut, while the top\par \par \uc2 quintile was estimated to receive a 2.9\par \par \uc2 percent increase in after-tax income.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DUEHREN\par \par \uc2 ''We have to remember that for\par \par \uc2 years in this country, Democrats\par \par \uc2 protested the results of elections.\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  in 2016 said that\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had the election\par \par \uc2 stolen by \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  because\par \par \uc2 the Russians bought like $500,000\par \par \uc2 worth of \uc2 Facebook\uc2  ads.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This is misleading.\par \par \uc2 It is true that Democratic lawmakers\par \par \uc2 have objected to counting a state's electors\par \par \uc2 after the elections of recent Republican\par \par \uc2 presidents in 2001, 2005 and 2017. But\par \par \uc2 in those cases, the losing candidate had\par \par \uc2 already conceded, did not try to overturn\par \par \uc2 election results and did not attempt to\par \par \uc2 persuade the vice presidents at the time\par \par \uc2 to halt proceedings as Mr. Trump is accused\par \par \uc2 of doing in 2020. And \uc2 Hillary Clinton\par \par \uc2 has said repeatedly that Russian interference\par \par \uc2 was partly to blame for her\par \par \uc2 defeat in the 2016 presidential election,\par \par \uc2 but again, she did not organize slates of\par \par \uc2 false electors and pressure officials to\par \par \uc2 overturn voting results. LINDA QIU\par \par \uc2 The reason child care is ''so\par \par \uc2 expensive right now is because\par \par \uc2 you've got way too few people\par \par \uc2 providing this very essential\par \par \uc2 service.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This requires context.\par \par \uc2 It is true that there are shortages of child\par \par \uc2 care centers and workers in many regions\par \par \uc2 of the country, in part because the\par \par \uc2 job pays poorly: The hourly wage is currently\par \par \uc2 lower in many instances than\par \par \uc2 wages in retail, food service or warehouses.\par \par \uc2 But Mr. Vance's proposal to provide\par \par \uc2 some financial support for informal\par \par \uc2 family care would most likely not fix\par \par \uc2 what is essentially a broken market. The\par \par \uc2 core problem is that the fees most parents\par \par \uc2 can afford to pay simply do not\par \par \uc2 cover the cost of doing business for\par \par \uc2 providers, with money left over for profit.\par \par \uc2 And the reason the cost of American\par \par \uc2 child care is so burdensome is that unlike\par \par \uc2 most other developed nations, the\par \par \uc2 United States government\uc2  does not\par \par \uc2 meaningfully subsidize the cost.\par \par \uc2 DANA GOLDSTEIN\par \par \uc2 ''This epidemic of violence, the\par \par \uc2 gross majority -- close to 90\par \par \uc2 percent in some of the statistics I've\par \par \uc2 seen -- of the gun violence in this\par \par \uc2 country is committed with illegally\par \par \uc2 obtained firearms.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This needs context.\par \par \uc2 It is difficult to discern the exact percentage\par \par \uc2 of illegally obtained guns used in\par \par \uc2 crime in the United States. The topic is\par \par \uc2 not well researched, and the situation\par \par \uc2 varies from state to state. In 2019, the\par \par \uc2 Justice Department published a survey\par \par \uc2 of prison inmates that found more than\par \par \uc2 half had either stolen their gun, found it\par \par \uc2 at the scene of the crime or obtained it on\par \par \uc2 the street or from the underground market.\par \par \uc2 Just 7 percent had bought it under\par \par \uc2 their own name from a licensed dealer.\par \par \uc2 But Mr. Vance made the comment after\par \par \uc2 being asked about how to curb mass\par \par \uc2 shootings in the United States, particularly\par \par \uc2 in schools. Mass shootings, which\par \par \uc2 account for fewer than 0.5 percent of all\par \par \uc2 gun homicides, are mostly committed\par \par \uc2 with legal weapons, according to a study\par \par \uc2 published in 2022 by the National Institute\par \par \uc2 of Justice, a research arm of the Justice\par \par \uc2 Department. The institute conducted\par \par \uc2 a detailed examination of the assailants\par \par \uc2 in 172 mass shootings from 1966\par \par \uc2 to 2019. It found that 77 percent of perpetrators\par \par \uc2 of mass shootings bought at least\par \par \uc2 some of their firearms legally, while illegal\par \par \uc2 purchases were made by 13 percent\par \par \uc2 of those committing mass shootings. In\par \par \uc2 cases involving K-12 school shootings,\par \par \uc2 more than 80 percent of individuals who\par \par \uc2 engaged in shootings stole guns from\par \par \uc2 family members. SHERYL GAY STOLBERG\par \par \uc2 ''We need to figure out how to solve\par \par \uc2 the inflation crisis caused by\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's policies.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This needs context.\par \par \uc2 Several studies have suggested that\par \par \uc2 spending under the Biden administration\par \par \uc2 in response to the pandemic did contribute\par \par \uc2 to inflation, but it was not the sole\par \par \uc2 or even primary driver of the rapid price\par \par \uc2 increases that started in 2021 and have\par \par \uc2 only recently faded.\par \par \uc2 Inflation jumped amid pandemicspurred\par \par \uc2 lockdowns that left goods in\par \par \uc2 short supply, and was exacerbated by\par \par \uc2 Russia's invasion of Ukraine. Studies\par \par \uc2 have found that the size of U.S. federal\par \par \uc2 spending did worsen the inflation --\par \par \uc2 some even find large effects -- but inflation\par \par \uc2 took off globally, not just in the\par \par \uc2 United States, in a sign that other factors\par \par \uc2 were also at play. JEANNA SMIALEK\par \par \uc2 ''The one thing that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did is\par \par \uc2 he continued some of the Trump\par \par \uc2 tariffs that protected American\par \par \uc2 manufacturing jobs.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This is true.\par \par \uc2 After carrying out a multiyear review of\par \par \uc2 the tariffs that Mr. Trump placed on\par \par \uc2 China, Mr. Biden largely decided to keep\par \par \uc2 those levies in place. The review, which\par \par \uc2 the Biden administration published last\par \par \uc2 month, quoted economic analyses that\par \par \uc2 have found that Mr. Trump's tariffs --\par \par \uc2 and the retaliatory tariffs that China has\par \par \uc2 imposed on American products -- had a\par \par \uc2 small negative effect on U.S. economic\par \par \uc2 welfare, positive impacts on U.S. production\par \par \uc2 in the industries most affected by\par \par \uc2 the tariffs and minimal effects on economywide\par \par \uc2 prices and employment.\par \par \uc2 ANA SWANSON\par \par \uc2 ''\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  could have\par \par \uc2 destroyed the program. Instead, he\par \par \uc2 worked in a bipartisan way to\par \par \uc2 ensure that Americans have access\par \par \uc2 to affordable care.''\par \par \uc2 MR. VANCE\par \par \uc2 This is false.\par \par \uc2 Even after the Senate tried and failed to\par \par \uc2 repeal the Affordable Care Act, the\par \par \uc2 Trump administration continued to take\par \par \uc2 actions that weakened the health care\par \par \uc2 law. Enrollment also declined under the\par \par \uc2 Trump administration, contrary to Mr.\par \par \uc2 Vance's claim that Americans did not\par \par \uc2 lose health care.\par \par \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  has previously\par \par \uc2 detailed several ways the Trump administration\par \par \uc2 was undermining the Affordable\par \par \uc2 Care Act, including by limiting outreach\par \par \uc2 and advertising, allowing the sale\par \par \uc2 of cheaper plans with fewer benefits and\par \par \uc2 reducing subsidies to insurance companies\par \par \uc2 for low-income enrollees.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration also said it\par \par \uc2 would stop defending crucial parts of the\par \par \uc2 health care law in court in 2018, and said\par \par \uc2 it believed that the law was unconstitutional\par \par \uc2 in 2019. Under the Trump administration,\par \par \uc2 the number of enrollees declined\par \par \uc2 to 11.4 million in 2020, from 12.7 million in\par \par \uc2 2016. LINDA QIU\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020241003eka30004d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
