\par\par \uc2 Foreign Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Buffer Zones On  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Are Coming Near Clinics\b0\par\par\uc2 By Megan Specia \par \uc2 818 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 September 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 5\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ''Safe access'' zones outside clinics in England and Wales will make it illegal to harass anyone seeking medical services or working there, the \uc2 British government\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Buffer zones will be introduced around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in England and Wales starting at the end of October, the \uc2 British government\uc2  said on Wednesday, in an effort to prevent the harassment of women using those services.\par \par \uc2 The new measures will prohibit protest within 150 meters -- nearly 500 feet -- of clinics or hospitals offering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, and make it illegal to hand out anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaflets in that buffer zone or block anyone from reaching a clinic. The penalty is a fine, with no upper limit.\par \par \uc2 As legal access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been curtailed in several countries around the world, most notably in the United States after the Supreme Court there overturned Roe v. Wade in 2022, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and academics in Britain say that protests at clinics in the country have increased.\par \par \uc2 In England and Wales, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is permitted up to 24 weeks of pregnancy, must be approved by two doctors, and can only be carried out under the care of a licensed clinic or \uc2 National Health Service\uc2  hospital. An \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be carried out after that time only if the mother's life is at risk or if the fetus has a severe abnormality.\par \par \uc2 Jess Phillips, a government minister, said in a statement that the buffer zones would combat ''harassment, abuse and intimidation as people exercise their legal right to health care.''\par \par \uc2 ''The right to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services is a fundamental right for women in this country, and no one should feel unsafe when they seek to access this,'' she said. ''For too long \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics have been without these vital protections, and this government is determined to do all we can do to make this country a safer place for women.''\par \par \uc2 The new measures formed part of a law that was passed under the previous Conservative government, the Public Order Act 2023, following a vote in Parliament that received broad cross-party support.\par \par \uc2 They will make it illegal for ''anyone to do anything that intentionally or recklessly influences someone's decision to use \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, obstructs them, or causes harassment or distress to someone using or working at these premises,'' according to the Home Office, the government department responsible for crime and policing.\par \par \uc2 The Home Office promised guidance for the police and prosecutors on how to enforce the law in the coming weeks, before the ''protection zones'' come into force.\par \par \uc2 The measures will bring England and Wales in line with other parts of the United Kingdom. Northern Ireland introduced a similar policy last year, and Scotland recently passed legislation creating buffer zones around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics that comes into force later this month.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 British Pregnancy Advisory Service\uc2 , a charity that provides \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care services including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  across Britain, has been campaigning for a decade for safe zones around clinics.\par \par \uc2 Heidi Stewart, its chief executive, said in a statement that the new measures ''can't come soon enough.''\par \par \uc2 ''For years our staff and the women we care for have endured anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fanatics standing outside clinics for hours on end, staring at them accessing or going to provide private medical care, stopping them outside and telling them that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is murder, handing out leaflets,'' she said, adding, ''We and Parliament have been clear that none of this behavior is acceptable outside a medical service.''\par \par \uc2 Catherine Robinson, a spokeswoman for Right To Life U.K., an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  charity, criticized the zones, saying that the group's volunteers had provided ''practical support'' to women outside \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics.\par \par \uc2 ''The implementation of buffer zones next month will mean that vital practical support provided by volunteers outside \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, which helps to provide a genuine choice, and offers help to women who may be undergoing coercion, will be removed for women and many more lives will likely be lost to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 Louise McCudden, U.K. head of external affairs at MSI Reproductive Choices, a charity that provides contraception and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, said some of its clinics' staff had witnessed a variety of harassment from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists.\par \par \uc2 ''The behavior we've seen outside our clinics includes spitting, calling women 'murderers,' crying out 'Mummy! Mummy!' to women as they enter or leave, filming or taking photographs, and handing out false medical information,'' Ms. McCudden said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The charity provides reproductive services in a number of countries around the world and Ms. McCudden noted that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protests outside their clinics had spiked after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade in 2022, ending five decades of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the United States.\par \par \uc2 ''Whatever your personal views are on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , nobody should be harassed while accessing health care,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page A5. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240919ek9j0004o\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 rst=nytf AND (abortion OR "reproductive rights" OR "reproductive health") AND (atleast5(abortion) OR atleast3("reproductive rights"))\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/30/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trq